From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoCo starter <coco-starter@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:59:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] trap: press scripted keys and report snapshot checkpoints

At every hit of the trap whose condition equals COCO_KEYS_AT, read the
next line of the file named by COCO_KEYS: XRoar key names separated by
spaces. Newly held keys are pressed and keys no longer held are
released through the keyboard API, which drives the emulated keyboard
matrix. At the end of the script every key is released. Each step logs
COCO_KEYS,<step>,<tick> on stderr, and the end logs
COCO_KEYS_END,<steps>,<tick>. An unknown key name logs
COCO_KEYS_UNKNOWN,<name> and exits with status 2.

When a trap writes the snapshot named by COCO_CHECKPOINT, log
COCO_CHECKPOINT,<tick>,<ticks per second> and ask the null UI's video
equipment to save the next complete frame.

Nothing here writes RAM, CPU registers or PIA state.

This is test equipment for the CoCo starter's scripts/coco.py.
